            <ArticleTitle>Portal vein thrombosis following laparoscopic gastric plication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e6-e7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/rcsann.2016.0250</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Portal vein thrombosis (PVT) following laparoscopic surgery including Roux-en-Y bypass, sleeve gastrectomy and Nissen's fundoplication is a rare but recognised complication. Laparoscopic gastric plication in a new procedure that is popular in some parts of the world. We report a case of a patient suffering PVT as a complication of this surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
